  "note": "A2 liść · rides a2_gen_pl, which lands immediately before it. CHECK RESULT: a1_shopping already owns every word on the original candidate list — cena, tani, drogi, płacić, kosztować, kasa, gotówka, karta, paragon, reszta, wyprzedaż, zniżka, portfel, pieniądze — plus kupować, sprzedawać, sklep, klient, torba, rozmiar, otwarty, zamknięty, za darmo, oferta, zwrot pieniędzy, kolejka, lada, portmonetka, przymierzać, targ, dom handlowy, funt, euro, dolar, cent. None of those are re-taught here; they are ANCHORS. This pack teaches the second layer: the physical money (moneta, banknot, bankomat), the bank side (konto, kredyt, płatność), the shop objects (koszyk, wózek, prezent), the person (sprzedawca), what you do with money (wydawać, zarabiać, oszczędzać) and rich/poor. DROGI/DROGA: both are already taught — drogi = expensive (a1_shopping), droga = road (a1_city), and blisko drogi is a live chunk. They are handled here by recycling drogi in a sentence with an explain that names the clash. FORKS: (1) złoty (the actual currency) is omitted — it declines adjectivally (pięć złotych) and a2_numbers_gen is not built, so teaching it would invite *pięć złoty*. (2) No numeral+noun phrases anywhere for the same reason. (3) Only citation forms are demanded — every noun here is masculine inanimate or neuter, so accusative = nominative for free; moneta and płatność are kept in the nominative so no untaught inflected form is ever required. Adjectives take no gender badge.",
